.TH "RTCERROR.RECEIVEDALERT" "3JS" "August 28, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
RTCError.receivedAlert \- RTCError: receivedAlert property
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This feature is available in Dedicated Web Workers.
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]receivedAlert\f[B]\f[R] read\-only property of the
\f[CR]RTCError\f[R] interface specifies the fatal DTLS error which
resulted in an alert being received from the remote peer.
.SH VALUE
A positive integer value.
.RS
.PP
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This property is \f[CR]null\f[R] if the
\f[CR]RTCError\f[R] doesn\(cqt represent a DTLS error.
DTLS errors are indicated by the \f[CR]errorDetail\f[R] property being
set to \f[CR]dtls\-failure\f[R].
.RE
